Z||000000||Formula||01-27-2000||03:02 PM||||I got your e-mail<P>I was wondering if you meant car audio or home audio.<P>I think you meant home so I'll explain what I did.<P>On the back of my stereo there is an rca out that I ran a standard Rca cable to a "Car audio Amplifier"  The amp is running off an old 12 v 6amp battery charger (with an on/off button).  Then you just plug the + and - sides of the speaker in to the amp and boom its done.  The only odd thing is that you have to splice a speaker wire from the 12v source to the REM screw.<P>If you were talking about a regular style subwoofer its usually just one rca cable and a plug.  But I prefer the bass of car audio stereos over conventional because they go a lot deeper.<P>Thats my 2 cents.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||01-27-2000||03:17 PM||||You're right, i was talking home audio.  I don't have an rca out on mine, that's what I was wondering about... I guess I could get an amp with speaker-level inputs but that would make it a little more complicated..  I'm with ya' on the preference, tho.  thanks a bunch!||||reg||1
